WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.011
The Emergencies Act invocation.

00:00:02.011 --> 00:00:07.704
February twenty twenty-two: the first-ever invocation of the Emergencies Act in Canadian history.

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:11.090
Two hundred and ten bank accounts frozen without court orders.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.488
Nine days of emergency powers.

00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:16.022
Zero charges for the invocation itself.

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:23.477
January twenty twenty-four: the Federal Court of Appeal ruled the invocation unreasonable and a violation of Charter rights.

00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:26.079
From protest to emergency to ruling.

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:29.977
January twenty twenty-two: Freedom Convoy protests begin.

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:35.215
February fourteenth: the Emergencies Act is invoked for the first time in Canadian history.

00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:38.056
Bank accounts are frozen without court orders.

00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:42.056
February twenty-third: the Act is revoked after nine days.

00:00:42.056 --> 00:00:44.090
A public inquiry follows.

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:49.170
January twenty twenty-four: the Federal Court rules the invocation was unreasonable.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.715
What the Federal Court found.

00:00:50.715 --> 00:01:00.147
Justice Mosley concluded the decision to issue the Proclamation does not bear the hallmarks of reasonableness — justification, transparency, and intelligibility.

00:01:00.147 --> 00:01:05.784
The Court found the invocation was not justified in relation to relevant factual and legal constraints.

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:14.818
Section 2(b) free expression, Section 8 unreasonable search, and Section 2(d) freedom of association were all violated.

00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:18.170
Despite this ruling, no personal accountability resulted.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.534
The precedent problem.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:28.806
Future governments now have a playbook: invoke emergency powers, freeze bank accounts, suppress protest, then revoke the Act before meaningful judicial review.

00:01:28.806 --> 00:01:31.556
The court ruling came two years after the fact.

00:01:31.556 --> 00:01:33.965
The bank accounts were already unfrozen.

00:01:33.965 --> 00:01:35.431
The damage was done.

00:01:35.431 --> 00:01:42.215
The precedent is set regardless of the ruling — governments know they can act first and face consequences later, if at all.
